(S4, L4 % 15 + "If apples are selling at Rs.40 per kg, how much can you buy for Rs.1200?", ["35 kg", "25 kg", "40 kg", "30 kg"], 3, "1200 / 40 = 30 kg.", "Tip: quantity = money divided by price per unit."),
(S4, L4 % 16 + "Sweet is to sour as cold is to:", ["Ice", "Hot", "Weather", "Snow", "Chill"], 1, "Sweet and sour are opposites, and the opposite of cold is hot.", "Tip: check whether an analogy is about opposites or about synonyms."),
(S4, L4 % 17 + "Which one of the following is different from others?", ["Salmon", "Fish", "Crab", "Shark", "Whale"], 1, "Salmon, crab, shark and whale are all specific sea animals, while Fish is the general category name. This follows the answer key (whale is also not a true fish).", ODD),
(S4, L4 % 18 + "Which letter comes next in the following series? B, F, I, M, P, ?", ["Q", "S", "T", "R"], 2, "The steps are +4, +3, +4, +3, so the next step is +4: P + 4 = T.", LET),
(S4, L4 % 19 + "A bakery sells a mixture of 2 parts cream and 3 parts milk. How many litres of cream will it take to make 15 litres of the mixture?", ["5 litres", "9 litres", "6 litres", "10 litres"], 2, "The mixture has 5 parts in total, so one part is 3 litres. Cream is 2 parts: 2 x 3 = 6 litres.", "Tip: add the parts of a ratio first, then divide the total by that sum."),
(S4, L4 % 20 + "Kund, Mora and Mokoma are three cities. Mora is 120 km in the west of Kund and Mokoma is 320 km in the North of Mora. Then Kund is in the ____ of Mokoma.", ["South", "North", "East", "North West", "South East"], 4, "Mokoma is directly north of Mora, and Kund is east of Mora. So Kund is to the south and east of Mokoma, which is South East.", "Tip: sketch a quick map with north at the top."),
(S4, L4 % 21 + "Which letter comes next in the following series? A, B, D, G, K, ?", ["N", "O", "P", "Q"], 2, "The steps are +1, +2, +3, +4, so the next step is +5: K + 5 = P.", LET),
(S4, L4 % 22 + "How many packs of envelopes can be bought for Rs.3 at the rate of 50 paisa each?", ["5", "7", "6", "3"], 2, "Rs.3 is 300 paisa, and 300 / 50 = 6 packs.", "Fact: 1 rupee equals 100 paisa."),
(S4, L4 % 23 + "In a college, out of 200 students 45% study Physics and 65% study Maths. Are there any students who neither study Physics nor Maths?", ["Yes", "No", "Uncertain"], 2, "Physics has 90 students and Maths 130, a total of 220, so at least 20 study both. If exactly 20 study both there are none who study neither, but if more study both there are some. The answer cannot be fixed (the paper key says Yes).", "Tip: when overlap is unknown, the number outside both sets can vary."),
(S4, L4 % 24 + "Which number comes next? 30, 25, 19, 12, ?", ["6", "5", "3", "4"], 3, "The differences are 5, 6, 7, so the next difference is 8: 12 - 8 = 4.", NUM),
(S4, L4 % 25 + "ADVANCE is to FORWARD as INCREASE is to:", ["Raise", "Recede", "Lower", "Decrease", "High"], 0, "Advance and forward are synonyms, and the synonym of increase is raise.", "Tip: decide whether the first pair is synonyms or opposites before choosing."),
(S4, L4 % 26 + "Which one of the following is different from the others?", ["Brazil", "Canada", "Chile", "New York", "Argentine"], 3, "Brazil, Canada, Chile and Argentina are countries. New York is a city.", ODD),
(S4, L4 % 27 + "Which number comes next? 3, 7, 12, 18, ?", ["23", "26", "25", "24"], 2, "The differences are 4, 5, 6, so the next difference is 7: 18 + 7 = 25.", NUM),
(S4, L4 % 28 + "All animals have tails. Some birds have tails. X has a tail, therefore it is a bird:", ["Yes", "No", "Uncertain"], 2, "Having a tail does not prove it is a bird, since every animal has a tail. So the conclusion is uncertain.", "Tip: a shared feature never proves membership of a smaller group."),
(S4, L4 % 29 + "A car is travelling at the speed of 120 km per hour. How many minutes will it take to travel 24 km?", ["15 minutes", "10 minutes", "12 minutes", "20 minutes"], 2, "120 km per hour is 2 km per minute, so 24 km takes 24 / 2 = 12 minutes.", "Tip: convert km per hour to km per minute by dividing by 60."),
